    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see your point, but some sociologists argue that secularism alone lacks the \"moral glue\" that religion provides, leading to atomization and a breakdown in community trust. They say a completely secular society can become too individualistic and lose its sense of collective responsibility. How do you weigh that against the benefits of a secular state?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
